WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.319
The overall theme of the film, that I got from
anyway, was about a young girl, you know,

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:07.680
trying to find her purpose and trying to
figure out what she wants to do in life -

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:14.490
Yeah, which is kind of what we all go
through. Right! So it's really relatable

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.420
like especially when I was watching it I was like, God I can really relate to that.
Have you ever been in a point like that

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.780
yourself what have you always known what
you want to do? Totally not, and I think

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.600
that's why I kind of relate and I think
most people do. You know when I was

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:33.750
probably around, she's 20 when we meet her
in the film, and that was probably

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:39.360
during the time when I was working in
a Levi's store, I'd quit ballet school

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.710
which I thought was my gonna be my path
but I, my gut instinct told me that I

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.670
want to do something different I had
tried out for theatre school and I

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:56.430
didn't come in four times and I was going to go to university and I just remember 'cause I met I still kind of have

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:02.370
the same close friends that I met
when I was like 18, 17 and we said now

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:06.000
because now we're getting closer to 30
and I'm like "do you remember where we

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.570
just wanted to fast-forward?" 'cause I just
wanted to it was like so what is gonna

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:13.799
you know I just didn't know, what was
gonna happen and but that is also part

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:18.360
of I think a very important time when
you you also get to try different things

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.530
and I think like Lara in this film you
shouldn't feel pressured - a lot of people

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.340
around her telling her "you should step
into, you know the shoes of your dad,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:30.750
you should follow his path" and she you
know, she says "no I'm not gonna". I mean

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:34.860
and she has a manor and all the riches
in the world but she wants to really, you

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.750
know, do her own thing and
find her own footing and find her own

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.770
path. You obviously had to do a lot of
physical training I can imagine for this

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:48.689
film. Yeah... You looked amazing.
Could you talk me through like, what

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:53.340
was your routine like in the gym and how
often did you train? Well yeah I mean it

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.219
was so many different skills of course
that I practiced for this role but I

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:00.390
also to be able to gain I gained about
10, 12 pounds of muscle and I had a

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:04.380
Magnet, my trainer who I worked with for
four months leading up to it

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.429
and then every day before I started to
film I was in the gym and something that

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:12.000
I learned was you know I've done much
more kind of yoga and Pilates and a lot

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.710
of cardio but
I started to integrate a lot more muscle

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:20.500
training a lot more and that is still do
none of the same level I did of course for the film but

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:24.850
that was something that I really enjoyed
I felt very much in my body and I loved

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:29.020
having another kind of strength.
Yeah and how often did you train, was it like every

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:34.300
day? It's five to six days a week. So pretty much every day. Yeah and then

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:40.720
Sundays was pizza day. Pizza day oh yeah, I bet you were waiting for Sundays to come around! No I think the first

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:49.510
thing I said when I woke up was "It's pizza day!" Do you have any like
quirky health or bonus tips that you did

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:55.180
during training? Or just in general? Yeah it's one of those things I know is

00:02:55.180 --> 00:03:00.400
when I travel a lot like sleep. Oh my god
it changes the way you look, the way you

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:06.970
feel and the way, you know, how
you just feel generally in life at the

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:10.390
moment you know so that's something that
I know myself I'm like my mum used to

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.600
tell me when I was kid and when she said
I had to go to bed at 7:30,

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.250
I said "why?" she was like "well 'cause you do
get a bit grumpy when you don't have routines" and then I

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:24.690
realised when I'm old I was like, that is
actually true, mum. Speaking of like

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:31.150
the way you look and beauty and you know wellness and things like that, you obviously are doing lots of travel for the job,

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.440
do you have any like products and skincare things that you use?
Yeah because I mean of course now I have a

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.549
wonderful professional team to make me look, 
you know put on my makeup for camera

00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:45.790
and things but I very rarely use makeup
in my everyday life but I I love

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:51.549
skincare and if anything my skin goes
extremely dry so you will find me, I can

00:03:51.549 --> 00:03:56.799
put like hand cream in my face
and it still kind of goes in so on flights and

00:03:56.799 --> 00:04:01.810
things I always put on like masks or I
have I always have a night cream as my

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:06.060
day cream. That could work.

